*               GROUPSTORE new IN string USING i, n {, delimiter}.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !GROUPSTORE(rep, s, i, n, d)
*
* Replaces, inserts or deletes the delimited substrings of S, which is changed in place: it does what
* S = FIELDSTORE(S, d, i, n, rep) does, as the manual says GROUPSTORE does.  The statement supplies a field mark when no
* delimiter was written.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

subroutine !groupstore(rep, s, i, n, d)
$catalog !groupstore

   s = fieldstore(s, d, i, n, rep)
   return
end

* END-CODE
